  "problem": "$\\frac{5}{3}\\times \\frac{1}{10}=$",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{3}\\times \\frac{1}{10}=\\frac{5\\times 1}{3\\times 10}=\\frac{5}{30}\n$$\n\nWe reduce this fraction to its simplest form by dividing the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{30}=\\frac{5÷5}{30÷5}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$",
